# Coding Style

- Keep it short. Add a file or method only when it has its own job
- Names are in English. Namespace `_Project.Develop.Runtime.<Area>`. No comments or summaries. Delete agent/TODO noise when touching a file
- Do not null-check anything that always comes from DI or a factory. Missing wiring fails loudly
- Real state uses a concrete check in the script (unequipped, destroyed, disposed), not `== null`
- No `?.` or `ArgumentNullException` “just in case”

## Commits

- Match repo style: `feat:` / `fix:` / short why-focused subject
- Only commit when the user asks

## Answers to the user

- Direct and concise; Russian if the user writes in Russian
- No long recaps of what you “will do”; show outcomes
